            "question": "Will the hardware hold up to salt air in Carlsbad Village and Terramar?",
            "answer": "<p>The spigots, connectors, hinges and latches are 2205 marine-grade stainless steel, which carries a 10-year no-rust promise. Both finishes, Brushed Stainless and Matte Black, sit on that same alloy. The tempered glass does not corrode; it collects a salt film that rinses off with fresh water. Hose the hardware when you wash the windows and it stays bright a block from the beach.</p>",
