        "t1": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Carlsbad projects: ocean views, lagoons and pool yards</strong></p><p>Carlsbad runs about seven miles along the coast between Oceanside and Encinitas, and three lagoons cut inland through it: Buena Vista, Agua Hedionda and Batiquitos. Homes in the Village and along Carlsbad Boulevard face the ocean. Homes in Terramar and around the lagoons face the water from a bluff or a slope. On those lots a frameless glass deck railing is chosen for one reason: nothing stands between the sofa and the horizon.</p><p>Inland, La Costa, Aviara, Bressi Ranch and Rancho Carrillo are newer tracts with backyard pools, second-floor balconies and HOA architectural review. There we ship 60\" glass pool fences, 48\" balcony railings and stair glass for interior remodels. Oceanside, Vista and San Marcos customers order the same parts, and the freight carrier delivers to all of them.</p>"
          }
        },
        "t2": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Salt air, marine layer and the hardware that handles it</strong></p><p>Salt air reaches well past the beach in Carlsbad, and the marine layer keeps surfaces damp for much of May and June. Salt is hard on plated and painted steel. Every spigot, connector, hinge and latch we sell is 2205 marine-grade stainless steel with a 10-year no-rust promise. The 12 mm tempered panels have a lifetime warranty against manufacturing defects. A rinse with fresh water now and then keeps the finish bright, in Brushed Stainless or Matte Black.</p><p>The California code sets 42\" as the minimum guard height, even for houses. The City of Carlsbad building division applies the 2022 Title 24 codes. The 46\" panel gives a 48\" railing and is the common choice for ocean-view decks. Parts of the city sit in the coastal zone, so ask the building division whether your address needs a coastal review. Details are on the <a href=\"/pages/california-building-standards-code-for-glass-railings\">California code page</a>.</p>"
          }
        },
        "t3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Delivery to Carlsbad and DIY installation</strong></p><p>Orders are processed in 2–3 business days, then delivered in 5–10 business days by freight carrier with liftgate delivery. The driver lowers the crate at the curb. Plan for a clear spot on the street in the Village or on the driveway in La Costa. The price at checkout is final, with no duties or tariffs, and orders over 3,000 USD ship free. Check the glass on arrival and report any damage within 3 days, before installation, for a free replacement or refund.</p><p>The system is designed for DIY installation. Each panel sits in two spigots, with no posts. Most standard installations take about 4 hours with the <a href=\"/pages/glass-railing-installation-guide\">installation guide</a> and videos. Spigots fix to wood joists or a concrete slab with screws sold separately. Engineering documents for both substrates are available for your permit file.</p>"
          }
        }
